when youre modifying the game's code, its best practice to make your changes as plugins instead of directly modifying the file. there are a handful of reasons for it, but keeping track of the changes youve made is exactly one of them.
its not a fancy process. you just take the functions with your added changes, save them as a .js file, place it in your project's js/plugins folder, load it as a plugin, and save your project. your changes will be applied.

