the error is a little different than youre thinking. its not that states is undefined, its that engine cannot read the states of undefined. meaning at some point, some function is looking for the states of a battler and it cannot find that battler. its difficult to say much more without seeing the error trace.
Playing around VS plugins is always tricky because of they make changes that are obfuscated. are you sure that your alias is working in general? also makeTargets() also does nothing by itself. it validates the targets for the skill, but it doesnt set the BattleManager's _targets by itself.
but since we're dealing with BS battle core, you will not be able to alter the contents of apply(). Which means you cant remove the applyItemUserEffect call within apply that is called on every hit of a skill if they still have it there.
you might be able to to look towards applyItemUserEffect instead. try typing
Code:
Game_Action.prototype.applyItemUserEffect
into the console to see what it is during gameplay. It may be unchanged. if it is, then you can use the second method i mentioned in my first post
